-Dimensions-at-Least-Three-September-23-2026.html#cor:coexistence","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:54e9db9336055e3b0332355c93f2cba0ba4b74728aa2dd500b215c894a74f0bd","file":"preprints/Absolutely-Continuous-Spectrum-for-Weak-Disorder-Anderson-Models-in-Dimensions-at-Least-Three-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex","line":250,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"094a3af115f6715eeaec6e2cf12c2ff4f4bfa9e55f73c41eca3972e15a6094d5","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Absolutely-Continuous-Spectrum-for-Weak-Disorder-Anderson-Models-in-Dimensions-at-Least-Three-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:54e9db9336055e3b0332355c93f2cba0ba4b74728aa2dd500b215c894a74f0bd","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Absolutely-Continuous-Spectrum-for-Weak-Disorder-Anderson-Models-in-Dimensions-at-Least-Three-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex#L250"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:coexistence}\nFor every fixed $d\\ge3$ and every fixed $0<\\lambda<\\lambda_d$,\nthere is a deterministic number $\\delta_{d,\\lambda}\\in(0,\\lambda/2]$\nsuch that the open interval\n\\[\n J_{d,\\lambda}\n =(-2d-\\lambda,-2d-\\lambda+\\delta_{d,\\lambda})\n\\]\nis disjoint from $I_d$ and, almost surely, both\n$\\chi_{I_d}(H_{\\lambda,\\omega})$ and\n$\\chi_{J_{d,\\lambda}}(H_{\\lambda,\\omega})$ are nonzero.\nThe restriction to $I_d$ is purely absolutely continuous, whereas the\nrestriction to $J_{d,\\lambda}$ is pure point with exponentially decaying\neigenfunctions. The probability-one event may depend on $d$ and $\\lambda$."}
